IMPORT prelude

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore) -- PART 2, ss 15 to 18A.
--
-- The rest of Part 2, after the termination and dismissal rules already encoded
-- in ea-part2.l4. These sections do two things: s 15 gives the employee one
-- further route out, s 16 fixes what a breach costs, and ss 18 and 18A keep the
-- CONTINUITY of a period of employment across changes of employer.
--
-- Continuity is why these matter and are not mere machinery: every band in the
-- s 10(3) notice table, and the qualifying periods for retrenchment and
-- retirement benefits in Part 4, are measured in length of service. ss 18 and
-- 18A decide whether that clock is reset when the employer changes.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No
-- pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate.

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 2, sections 15 to 18A`

§§ `15 -- Termination by employee threatened by danger`

-- s 15: "An employee may terminate his or her contract of service with his or
-- her employer WITHOUT NOTICE where the employee or the employee's dependant is
-- IMMEDIATELY THREATENED by danger to the person BY VIOLENCE OR DISEASE that
-- the employee DID NOT BY HIS OR HER CONTRACT OF SERVICE UNDERTAKE TO RUN."
--
-- Four conditions, all of them cumulative: the threat must be immediate, it
-- must be to the person, it must be violence or disease, and it must be a risk
-- outside what the contract undertook. The last limb is what keeps a nurse or a
-- security guard from relying on it for the ordinary risks of the job.
DECLARE DangerFacts HAS
    `the threat is to the employee or the employee's dependant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the danger is immediate`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the danger is to the person`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the danger is by violence or disease`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee undertook by the contract of service to run that risk` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DangerFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee may terminate without notice under section 15` IF
        `the facts`'s `the threat is to the employee or the employee's dependant`
    AND `the facts`'s `the danger is immediate`
    AND `the facts`'s `the danger is to the person`
    AND `the facts`'s `the danger is by violence or disease`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the employee undertook by the contract of service to run that risk`

§§ `16 -- Liability on breach of contract`

-- s 16: "SUBJECT TO ANYTHING IN THE CONTRACT OF SERVICE TO THE CONTRARY, the
-- party who breaks the contract of service is liable to pay to the other party
-- a sum EQUAL TO THE AMOUNT the firstmentioned party would have been liable to
-- pay UNDER SECTION 11 had the firstmentioned party terminated the contract of
-- service without notice or with insufficient notice."
--
-- So the measure of damages for breach is the payment in lieu of notice: the
-- salary that would have accrued over the notice period. Note the opening
-- words -- unlike s 8, which strikes down a contract term less favourable to the
-- employee, s 16 YIELDS to the contract in either direction.
GIVEN `the gross daily rate of pay` IS A NUMBER
    , `the notice period that governs, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the sum payable on breach under section 16` IS
    `the gross daily rate of pay` TIMES `the notice period that governs, in days`

-- "Subject to anything in the contract of service to the contrary": where the
-- contract provides its own measure, that governs instead.
GIVEN `the contract provides a different measure` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the contractual measure` IS A NUMBER
    , `the gross daily rate of pay` IS A NUMBER
    , `the notice period that governs, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount recoverable for breach` IS
    IF   `the contract provides a different measure`
    THEN `the contractual measure`
    ELSE `the sum payable on breach under section 16`
             `the gross daily rate of pay` `the notice period that governs, in days`

§§ `17 -- Trade union rights cannot be restricted by contract`

-- s 17: "Subject to any other written law for the time being in force, NOTHING
-- IN ANY CONTRACT OF SERVICE RESTRICTS, IN ANY WAY, the right of any employee
-- who is a party to such contract -- (a) to join a registered trade union;
-- (b) to participate in the activities of a registered trade union, whether as
-- an officer of the trade union or otherwise; or (c) to associate with any
-- other persons for the purpose of organising a trade union in accordance with
-- the provisions of the Trade Unions Act 1940."
--
-- Expressed as a statement about contracts rather than as a prohibition on
-- employers, so the rule is about whether a purported restriction has effect.
DECLARE PurportedRestriction HAS
    `on joining a registered trade union`                   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `on participating in the activities of a registered trade union` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `on associating with others to organise a trade union under the Trade Unions Act 1940` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)

GIVEN `the restriction` IS A PurportedRestriction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contractual restriction has no effect under section 17` IF
        `the restriction`'s `on joining a registered trade union`
    ..  `the restriction`'s `on participating in the activities of a registered trade union`
    OR  `the restriction`'s `on associating with others to organise a trade union under the Trade Unions Act 1940`

§§ `18 and 18A -- continuity of the period of employment`

-- s 18 preserves continuity in three cases, s 18A in a fourth. In every one the
-- formula is the same: the earlier period "counts as a period of employment
-- with" the new employer, and the change "does not break the continuity of the
-- period of employment".
DECLARE EmployerChange HAS
    -- s 18(1): a statutory substitution of one body corporate for another.
    `a body corporate was substituted as employer by or under written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 18(2): the employer died and the employee was taken into the employment
    -- of the personal representatives or trustees.
    `the employer died and the employee was taken into the employment of the personal representatives or trustees` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 18(3): a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees.
    `there was a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees who employ the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 18A(1): an undertaking or part of one was transferred.
    `an undertaking or part of one was transferred from one person to another` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the change` IS AN EmployerChange
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 18A applies to the change` IF
        `the change`'s `an undertaking or part of one was transferred from one person to another`
    AND `the change`'s `the employee was employed by the transferor in the undertaking or part transferred`

GIVEN `the change` IS AN EmployerChange
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the continuity of the period of employment is preserved` IF
        `the change`'s `a body corporate was substituted as employer by or under written law`
    ..  `the change`'s `the employer died and the employee was taken into the employment of the personal representatives or trustees`
    ..  `the change`'s `there was a change in the partners, personal representatives or trustees who employ the person`
    OR  `section 18A applies to the change` `the change`

-- s 18A(1)(a): the transfer "DOES NOT OPERATE TO TERMINATE the contract of
-- service ... but such contract of service has effect after the transfer AS IF
-- ORIGINALLY MADE between the person so employed and the transferee".
GIVEN `the change` IS AN EmployerChange
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer does not terminate the contract of service` IF
    `section 18A applies to the change` `the change`

-- s 18A(2): on completion, the transferor's rights, powers, duties and
-- liabilities pass, and acts or omissions on either side before the transfer
-- are deemed done by or in relation to the transferee. So the transferee
-- inherits not only the contract but its history.
GIVEN `the change` IS AN EmployerChange
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `acts and omissions before the transfer are deemed to be the transferee's` IF
    `section 18A applies to the change` `the change`

-- s 18A(3): "it is declared FOR THE AVOIDANCE OF DOUBT that the terms and
-- conditions of service ... are THE SAME as those enjoyed by the employee
-- immediately prior to the transfer."
GIVEN `the change` IS AN EmployerChange
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the terms and conditions of service are unchanged by the transfer` IF
    `section 18A applies to the change` `the change`

-- s 18A(5): before the transfer the TRANSFEROR must notify the affected
-- employees and any trade union of three things, so that consultation can take
-- place; s 18A(6) requires the TRANSFEREE to give the transferor the
-- information needed to do it. The duty is on the transferor and the knowledge
-- is with the transferee, which is why (6) exists.
DECLARE TransferNotice HAS
    `the fact, approximate date and reasons for the transfer were notified` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (5)(a)
    `the implications and the measures the transferor envisages were notified` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (5)(b)
    `the measures the transferee envisages were notified` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (5)(c)
    `the transferee gave the transferor the information needed` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (6)

GIVEN `the notice` IS A TransferNotice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transferor has discharged the section 18A(5) duty` IF
        `the notice`'s `the fact, approximate date and reasons for the transfer were notified`
    AND `the notice`'s `the implications and the measures the transferor envisages were notified`
    AND `the notice`'s `the measures the transferee envisages were notified`

GIVEN `the notice` IS A TransferNotice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transferee has discharged the section 18A(6) duty` IF
    `the notice`'s `the transferee gave the transferor the information needed`
